    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74008.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, it's hard to say. I mean, there are so many loopholes in that bill will make your head spend, which is why you can say one thing, it does X, but then with the loophole, it now does Y or doesn't do what you say it's going to do. And that's the thing. There was actually no cap to the debt ceiling. They're going to set into law record high levels of spending set during COVID, which is for an emergency only. And it's untenable for the taxpayers. I mean, we're going to go broke. And if you look at two years from now, like tax cuts and jobs act, that's going to expire. So taxes are going to go up if we don't sustain that. And what they didn't tell you, they want to tell you that there was a $2 trillion cut to the deficit over the next 10 years, but they didn't tell you that it's going to add $18.8 trillion to the debt. meaning that net net you're still adding 17.3 trillion dollars because it wasn't a two trillion dollar cut to the deficit was only 1.5 over 10 years and you're out you're still adding over 17 trillion dollars to the debt and so it's just one big lie and I just you know when I was at the Citadel the military college of South Carolina they taught us a cadet doesn't lie cheater steel or tolerate those who do and I'm not gonna lie to the American people I'm not gonna lie to the people of South Carolina my great state my home state and that that that what leadership was saying wasn't the",
