    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "And we're setting that $6 trillion more or less into law as the baseline spending for our country. going forward and then and then it grows government by about 1% a year we were republicans are bragging about work requirements but guess what CBO the congressional budget office said actually the because of the work requirements and the way the bill was written we're going to get more people on government welfare not less and you know it's just it's atrocious that you know the american people were sort of better lies on this thing and As you mentioned, Joe, when we got on here, more Democrats and Republicans voted for it. The Republicans gave up everything for nothing. And I can't believe that this happened, that we allowed this to happen. I don't want to hear a single Republican or Democrat talk about how they're going to save our country fiscally. because Republicans and Democrats alike are the ones that have run up the scorecard, they've run up spending, and they have no plan to stop it. And both parties this week caused what's going to happen over the next 10 years. It's untenable.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
